#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Turn ordinary tracks into Native Instruments .stem.mp4 files for Mixxx 2.6+.

Pipeline per track (default model "ft2sw"):
  1. ffmpeg decodes the source to a float32 44.1k stereo wav (the mix)
  2. mel_band_roformer_kim_ft2_bleedless_unwa (GPU, MSST) extracts vocals V
  3. inst = mix - V; BS-Roformer-SW (6-stem, MSST) splits inst, keeping drums D, bass B
  4. other = inst - D - B, so D+B+other+V == mix exactly (all float wav)
  5. ffmpeg muxes the original as stream 0 plus the four stems as streams 1-4
  6. the NI stem manifest is injected as a moov.udta.stem atom

--json: one JSON object per stdout line (start, track_start, track_done,
track_failed, done) instead of the human lines; see README.
Why ft2sw: htdemucs_ft vocal SDR 8.33 vs ~11.1-11.3 for RoFormers (MVSep
multisong). ~95 s per 4-min track on the RTX 3060.

Mixxx wants exactly 5 streams, identical codec and sample rate, and finds the
stem labels/colours in that atom (falling back to the .stem.mp4 extension).
"""

